From 077df55d3e264b173cca2a1c317759a9e98d483b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gillinger <christian.gillinger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:05:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] genesys: fix ImagePipelineNodeExtract bytes-per-pixel for
 multi-channel rows

ImagePipelineNodeExtract::get_next_row_data() computed the bytes per
pixel as get_pixel_format_depth(format) / 8, which is the depth PER
CHANNEL. For a three-channel 16-bit format that is 2, so it copied one
third of each row and zero-padded the rest. Use get_pixel_row_bytes(
format, 1), the bytes of one whole pixel.

No in-tree model reached this node with a multi-channel format before the
GL126 infrared crop is the first, so no existing model's output changes;
it is a latent bug fixed ahead of the first user.
---
 backend/genesys/image_pipeline.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backend/genesys/image_pipeline.cpp b/backend/genesys/image_pipeline.cpp
index 8dae0c5..61d7e5f 100644
--- a/backend/genesys/image_pipeline.cpp
+++ b/backend/genesys/image_pipeline.cpp
@@ -740,7 +740,11 @@ bool ImagePipelineNodeExtract::get_next_row_data(std::uint8_t* out_data)
             set_raw_pixel_to_row(out_data, i + x_src_width, RawPixel{}, format);
         }
     } else {
-        std::size_t bpp = get_pixel_format_depth(format) / 8;
+        // bytes per PIXEL: the format depth is per channel (RGB161616 = 16),
+        // so depth / 8 copied one third of a 3-channel row and zero-padded
+        // the rest (found by the GL126 IR crop, which is the first user of
+        // this node on a multi-channel format)
+        std::size_t bpp = get_pixel_row_bytes(format, 1);
         if (x_src_width > 0) {
             std::memcpy(out_data, cached_line_.data() + offset_x_ * bpp,
                         x_src_width * bpp);
-- 
